## 4. Accessibility Requirements

### REQ-11-ACC-01: Keyboard Navigation

**WHEN** a keyboard-only user interacts with the canvas, **THE SYSTEM SHALL** provide keyboard-accessible alternatives for all canvas operations.

- Tab navigates between: toolbar buttons, canvas area, layer list (left sidebar)
- When canvas is focused: arrow keys nudge, Delete deletes, Ctrl+Z undoes, Ctrl+A selects all
- All toolbar buttons are reachable via Tab and actionable via Enter/Space
- Context menu is openable via Shift+F10 or Menu key when an element is focused
- ARIA live region announces selection changes (e.g., "Text element selected", "3 elements selected")
- Focus indicator visible on all interactive elements (MUI default focus ring)
- Keyboard shortcut help dialog accessible via `?` key (lists all shortcuts with i18n `shortcuts.*` labels)

### REQ-11-ACC-02: Screen Reader Support

- Canvas container has `role="application"` with `aria-label` from `aria.canvasLabel` key
- Each element has `aria-label` with element type and position (interpolated `aria.elementLabel`: "Text element at position 100, 200")
- Selection state change announced via `aria-live="polite"` region using `aria.elementSelected` pluralization
- Drag announcements: `aria.dragging` interpolates real-time x/y coordinates via SR live region
- Resize announcements: `aria.resizing` interpolates width/height via SR live region
- Rotation announcements: `aria.rotating` interpolates angle via SR live region
- Rulers have `aria-hidden="true"` (decorative, not meaningful as text)
- Grid lines have `aria-hidden="true"`
- Zoom level displayed in a `aria-live` region when changed
- Unsaved changes warning is a `role="alert"` dialog
- Version conflict dialog is a `role="alertdialog"` with focus trap

### REQ-11-ACC-03: Color Contrast

- Selection border: `theme.palette.primary.main` — NO hardcoded colors anywhere
- Alignment guides: `theme.palette.primary.main` — visible against all background types
- Grid lines: `theme.palette.divider` color — subtle but visible
- Ruler markings: `theme.palette.text.secondary` on background
- Read-only banner: `theme.palette.warning.main` background with `theme.palette.warning.contrastText`

---

## 5. Knowledge Base & Progress Tracking

### REQ-11-KB-01: Canvas Implementation Documentation

**WHEN** the canvas implementation is complete, **THE SYSTEM SHALL** document the canvas coordinate system, pointer-event flow, and snap logic in `docs/frontend/canvas-editor.md`.

- Document coordinate conversion formula (screen ↔ template coordinates)
- Document pointer event lifecycle (pointerdown → pointermove → pointerup) for each interaction type
- Document undo/redo history strategy
- Document snap-to-grid and snap-to-element threshold values

### REQ-11-KB-02: AGENTS.md Update

**WHEN** the canvas store and components are finalized, **THE plan's tasks SHALL** update `frontend/views/AGENTS.md` (or create a canvas-specific instruction file) with:
- Canvas store conventions (no persistence, history stack with past/future, `string[]` for `selectedIds` NOT `Set`)
- Element component memoization pattern (`React.memo` per element, keyed by element ID)
- Pointer Events usage requirement (no HTML5 drag-and-drop)
- Coordinate system reference (96 DPI, template-pixel coordinates)
- react-zoom-pan-pinch integration (TransformWrapper ref, `onTransformed` → store sync)
- Permission keys: `certificates.templates.manage` (edit), `certificates.templates.view` (read-only)
- v1 constraints: no resize-while-rotated, no group resize/rotate, 6 element types only

